[[Christien Meindertsma]] with [[Enkev]], Netherlands, 2015.

Flax fiber and [[PLA]] pressed into one flat panel: four layers of woven flax textile and five layers of felted flax. The PLA is in the woven layers, alongside the long flax fibers. The soft stack is heat pressed, "melting the flax and PLA into the shape of a rigid chair."

The seat is cut and molded from the panel. What's left over becomes the legs.

It can be shredded and pressed again. At the very end it can be composted.

The flax came from her Flax Project, which began when she bought a Dutch farm's whole harvest.
